    "created_at": "2022-02-04T20:24:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-04T20:24:44Z",
    "body": "I can confirm the same thing is happening to me. This regression is breaking my configuration for `$git_status`. I'm mirroring the format of the official `git-prompt.sh`, which uses `%` to display tracked files.\r\n\r\nFor those using Nix, you can target the last working version of Starship with the following overlay:\r\n\r\n```nix\r\npkgs.starship.overrideAttrs (oldAttrs: rec {\r\n  pname = \"starship\";\r\n  version = \"0.58.0\";\r\n  src = pkgs.fetchFromGitHub {\r\n    owner = \"starship\";\r\n    repo = pname;\r\n    rev = \"v${version}\";\r\n    sha256 = \"sha256-s84fIpCyTF7FrJZGATjIJHt/+aknlhlz1V9s+c4f+Ig=\";\r\n  };\r\n  cargoDeps = oldAttrs.cargoDeps.overrideAttrs (lib.const {\r\n    name = \"${pname}-${version}-vendor.tar.gz\";\r\n    inherit src;\r\n    outputHash = \"sha256-5YOF0nXn4rdp3uxatzdvaqdAbLlHK6nq5H4+ZX/7joM=\";\r\n  });\r\n})\r\n```\r\n",
